title: "AI Action Paths (AAP): From Human–AI Collective Learning to Autonomous Brain Unit Societies"

message: >
If you use this repository in your research, engineering, educational,
or strategic work, please cite it using the metadata below.

type: report

authors:

* family-names: Tan
  given-names: Sizhe

abstract: >
AI Action Paths (AAP) introduces a structural framework for studying
the long-term evolution of Artificial Intelligence through Action Paths.
Rather than organizing AI solely around model architectures or benchmark
performance, AAP studies how AI continuously expands its participation
within Human–AI Civilization. The framework introduces the Height–
Breadth–Depth (HBD) Evaluation Matrix and describes the evolution from
LLM Scaling, Human–AI Discussion, Brain Units, and AI Freelance Workers
toward Unknown Gap Detection, Hybrid AI Organizations, and future
Human–AI Civilization.

